This distribution builds a C++ extension from first-party source, and vendors
one third-party artifact. Paths below are as packaged in the wheel, which is
the published distribution; in the source tree they sit under src/.

sdm_relational_engine/rfm/assets/mermaid.min.js
-----------------------------------------------

mermaid 11.15.0, MIT licensed, bundled so that Graph.visualize() renders a
graph offline in notebook environments that block external scripts. The bundle
is upstream bytes, unmodified; its SHA-256 is pinned in rfm/assets/VENDORED.md
and asserted by tests/test_vendored_mermaid.py. Its own components are
enumerated in the third-party section of LICENSE, and its licence text is in
rfm/assets/MERMAID_LICENSE.

The wire types this driver speaks to the model with are first-party source in
this distribution, under sdm_relational_engine/api; see its SOURCE.md.
Everything else, including the Predictive Query Language and the Universal TFM
wire types, is resolved by the package manager at install time.
